    "scope": "One automatic capture write-authority boundary adds read-only configured installation actor preparation, current native workspace/socket/catalog admission around native Write authorization and an in-process AgentCapturePublisher adapter. Exact new actor regression precedes the native service/receipt fixture, all direct server capture admission tests, shared CLI spool/native-publication/local-recovery consumers and affected/direct-consumer all-target checks/lint. Disabled preparation does not read identity or create state; effective Write/Admin and root changes keep the actor stable, other installation/purpose identities differ and captured native agent labels never authenticate. Binding denies catalog-only nonexistent manifests and removed registrations, and grants only Write even when server configuration permits Admin. Native preparation/publication and exact receipt replay preserve authenticated actor and code heads; read-only native requests deny both. The service adapter preserves bound/unbound request methods and existing RPC contracts; no permissive storage writer is added. New native repository creation already selects an empty AgentStore; legacy absent-domain initialization remains an explicit integration gate. This capability alone does not retain directory permission: the future worker must revalidate current admission before every publication and supervise deadlines, unknown outcomes, pause/restart and backpressure. Enabled server startup remains guarded. M17.2 and aggregate M17 remain In progress; supervised worker, bounded multi-repository draining, Cursor/OpenCode readers, typed controls/UI, real harness/cold full-flow and the full M17.3-M17.7 roadmap remain pending. No startup, browser lifecycle, native/WAL implementation, installed service, credentials, real RustFS or deployment is changed; root aggregate/unrelated wider suites are out of scope."
  },
