    "formats": "Additive metadata-only repository/integration/source selector and one-through-256 batch bound. Existing CaptureDrainReport counts the entire shared queue; pending entries, reader progress, prepared request/receipt encodings, request identities, sanitization and native/local completion semantics are unchanged.",
    "revision": "enclosing Jujutsu change tvywvvwv",
    "scope": "One native spool selection behavior extracts the exact-intent publication/completion loop for reuse by strict whole-spool CLI and bounded shared-spool partition drains. Invalid bounds fail before the drain lease; matching LocalPrepared requests anywhere in the selected partition fail before preparation even outside the current bound. Filtering, ordering and truncation leave foreign native/local partitions untouched. Unknown outcomes stop only this call with durable exact intent; mismatch/cancellation retain requests, release the global drain lease and retry without repreparation. Other processes may still enqueue while publication waits; existing cursor completion repairs durable reader progress before removal. Reports count all remaining entries and empty selections invoke no publisher. Selection grants no directory admission, write authority or scheduling fairness; the supervisor remains responsible for each. Exact regression, complete direct CLI publication/spool/local-recovery binaries, direct reader-progress cases, affected/direct-consumer all-target check/lint, formatting and architectural checks qualify this slice. M17.2 and aggregate M17 remain In progress; supervised automatic Codex composition, per-publication current admission, fair scheduling/deadlines/backpressure/controls, absent-domain initialization, pending-source recovery, Cursor/OpenCode readers, real harness/cold full-flow and the full M17.3-M17.7 roadmap remain pending. Startup guard remains in place. No model/RPC/WAL schema, browser lifecycle, credential, installed service, deployment or release behavior changed; root aggregate and unrelated wider suites are out of scope."
  },
