    "versions": "Rust 1.98.1; JJ 0.45.1; macOS ARM64. Synthetic qualified Codex CLI 0.156.1 transcript over actual native MemoryStore service/WAL/AgentStore, synthetic workspace/socket admission and pinned Kingfisher cache. A fixture reports unknown only after the real native publisher commits; this is not an actual network timeout, RustFS, live harness or whole-server cold startup proof.",
    "formats": "No production, dependency, native/source/admission/cursor/pending/prepared request/actor/receipt or wire format change. Existing exact prepared native bytes fill the configured physical byte budget; snapshots verify no mutation across revocation/pause/restart. Latest sanitized source progress remains unchanged on rejected ingress. Captured preparation overflow retains the current legacy hard-bound encoding unchanged until explicit configured capacity relief.",
    "revision": "enclosing Jujutsu change tzumtltr",
    "scope": "Qualifies a durable queue filled by a native prepared request after actual committed publication but caller acknowledgement loss. Its actor, request/publication/result/receipt identities remain exact. Current A revocation withholds receipt resolution and prevents A authority being borrowed from B. The full physical byte budget refuses B ingestion without durable cursor advancement, preserves exact queued bytes under repeated source/delivery steps and pause/restart, and retains activity admission for the offline B tail. Restoring A resolves the original receipt and frees capacity; B body and a later append then publish independently with sanitization. A's complete native AgentStore read snapshot and content remain unchanged after receipt replay, proving no reauthoring. An additional exact captured-growth case demonstrates the current strict byte-limit profile stages no selected native root/receipt and retains captured intent when Prepared replacement cannot fit; explicit capacity relief permits later publication. This confirms a relevant remaining startup gap: automatic new-capture admission must reserve bounded preparation headroom, with honest legacy diagnostics and native/local compatibility, while preserving hard byte bounds, dependent same-partition reduction and exact accepted intent. Canonical collaboration/CLI/verification and the M17.2 next action now name that gate. This slice does not claim headroom implementation or all durable queue pressure/fault qualification. Full direct supervisor binary is justified by its registered shared harness/context and lifecycle evidence; unrelated capture-runtime/CLI/UI/whole-Rust-workspace/root aggregate lanes are out of scope. M17/M17.2 remain In progress. Headroom admission, further queue/rotation/requalification/task-loss/deadline faults, process startup/ordered storage shutdown, legacy missing AgentStore initialization, Cursor/OpenCode readers, authenticated controls, coverage/backlog UI and real harness/cold qualification remain pending. M17.3-M17.7 remain pending. No installed service/binary, daemon restart, live harness process, credentials, checkpoints, deployment or publication changed. Automatic startup remains guarded."
  },
