    "scope": "Automatic reader ingress reserves bounded physical preparation space before durability and cursor acknowledgement. Native sizing permits every valid V1 delta shape through 4096 full-reference edits and the exact runtime acknowledgement plus explicit binding at maximum timestamp; it does not assume current projector output or author native requests. Local sizing uses the same pure request envelope as the local drainer and covers duplicated sanitized payload/profile/binding. Legal JSON whitespace makes the reservation visible to every existing physical-byte accounting handle without a compatibility marker or extra authority. Selected partition heads still prepare against current native roots in order; exact prepared retries and unknown receipts remain unchanged. Capacity refusal retains intent/cursors. Legacy queues are not rewritten; compact legacy overflow still stages no selected native root/receipt and needs explicit capacity relief. Original regression and all discovered fixture/invocation failures are recorded and resolved without weakened assertions; final recorded gates complete this narrow surface. Shared spool persistence and the common local request envelope justify the complete capture runtime and all direct native/server/CLI capture consumers; unrelated UI/whole-Rust-workspace/root aggregates remain out of scope. All previous 286 evidence entries remain unchanged. M17/M17.2 stay In progress. Remaining M17.2 gates include management diagnostics for legacy insufficient capacity, expanded pressure/rotation/retirement/requalification/task-loss/deadline faults, configured startup and ordered storage shutdown, legacy missing AgentStore initialization, Cursor/OpenCode readers, authenticated controls, coverage/backlog UI and live harness/cold qualification. M17.3-M17.7 remain pending. Automatic enabled startup stays guarded. No installed service/binary, daemon restart, credentials, checkpoint, harness execution, deployment or publication changed."
