    "versions": "Rust 1.98.1; JJ 0.45.1; macOS ARM64. Native MemoryStore and isolated Git-backed companion fixtures, synthetic Codex transcript and workspace/socket admission; no RustFS or live harness qualification.",
    "formats": "Supported native AgentRootV1, TranscriptChunkV1 and TranscriptManifestV1 encodings/identities remain unchanged. Local descriptor version 2 and transcript tail-page schema 2 are the supported profiles. Removed local descriptor version-1 upgrade and forward TranscriptPageV1 type/variant/re-export and read/append/audit compatibility. Obsolete formats are rejected without migration. Durable spool physical reservations, compact-record retry support, source cursors, exact requests and receipts are unchanged. Public generated OpenAPI remains identical.",
    "revision": "enclosing Jujutsu change lnkplqqz",
    "scope": "Implements the user decision to support only current AgentStore formats. Deletes the local descriptor in-memory upgrade, forward transcript type and shared compatibility branches including legacy source-receipt migration proof. Current prefix-before-tail read/audit/append preserves bounded ordering witnesses, other streams and complete selected closure audits. Converts service/HTTP/native-copy and model/WAL fixtures to current tails, reversing two-page construction to retain chronological prefixes. Replaces obsolete migration acceptance tests with meaningful current multi-stream/order and old-byte rejection regressions; historical evidence remains unchanged with explicit retired test references. Canonical chapters and current M17.2 next action remove missing-root initialization/migration gates and distinguish supported current V1-named root/chunk/manifest/provenance from obsolete formats. Native capture already requires its selected current root and keeps failing closed when absent; explicit first-use companion publication creates its current descriptor. No existing repositories are migrated or rewritten. Both new exact regressions failed before removal and pass afterward. Incorrect HTTP module qualifier matched zero tests; corrected exact case passes and no empty result is treated as qualification. Full affected model/WAL suites are justified by shared persistence across native/local consumers; direct service, CLI and supervisor consumers plus focused compile/lint/contracts/boundaries validate the impact surface. Existing publication facade only loses its obsolete re-export; behavioral modules remain below 300 lines. All previous 288 evidence entries preserved. M17/M17.2 and M13.3 stay In progress; M17.1 current-tail qualification stays Done. Remaining M17.2 includes compact spool capacity diagnostics, rotation/retirement/requalification/task-loss/deadline matrices, configured startup and ordered storage shutdown, Cursor/OpenCode readers, authenticated controls/UI and live/cold acceptance. M17.3-M17.7 remain pending. Automatic enabled startup remains guarded. No installed service/binary, daemon restart, credentials, checkpoint, deployment, live harness or publication changed. Root aggregate, unrelated UI, whole Rust workspace and real-storage lanes remain out of scope under targeted policy."
  },
