    "scope": "One physical-generation recovery behavior affects shared reader selection and sanitized enqueue plus native/local direct consumers. Automatic readers use the matching physical/header progress across every retained repository partition and pending entry; channel-wide generation and sequence floors are independent maxima. Generic sanitized pending entries also occupy allocation floors. Unchanged files do not alternate new generations. Delayed archived/current appends retain verified prefixes and allocate monotonic continuation generations without replaying acknowledged bytes. Truncation and equal-length rewrites reset offsets above all known generation floors. Fresh lease acquisition and ingress refresh bounds; final automatic admission is atomic under the mutation lock. Exact already-durable retries retain prior receipt/intent interpretation. Conflicting raw frames retain their identities/bytes and cannot enqueue or leak leases; complete pre-durability allocation liveness remains an explicit next gate. No accepted batch, ID, journal, prepared bytes or receipt is renumbered or rewritten. Generic APIs retain prior accepted generation semantics. Complete shared capture tests and direct native/server/CLI cursor, spool, publication, resume and parking consumers are justified by this common allocation boundary; UI, root aggregate, whole Rust workspace and real-storage lanes remain out of scope. All previous 292 evidence entries preserved. M17/M17.2 remain In progress, with raw-allocation liveness/races, wider rotation/root rebinding and task-loss/deadline faults, configured startup/ordered storage shutdown, Cursor/OpenCode readers, authenticated controls/coverage UI and real harness/cold qualification pending. M17.3-M17.7 remain pending. Automatic enabled startup remains guarded. No installed service/binary, unrelated daemon restart, credential, checkpoint, deployment or publication changed. Initial attempted canonical patch missed wrapped context and made no