    "remaining": [],
    "scope": "The explicit lifecycle driver owns the existing prepared supervisor and schedules discovery, admitted reading and exact delivery on retained independent blocking owners. Pause/resume uses one bounded internal command state; stop is terminal and ordered with synchronous dispatch. Timeout retains the join for later waiting; dropping the handle requests stop while its task drains. Driver errors also stop/drain remaining lanes before returning; a completed failed join is never repolled. Existing supervisor shutdown gains only an internal reusable stop path. This shared lifecycle change requires the complete direct supervisor suite, exact native runtime acceptance and underlying executor fault tests; server/CLI all-target compilation and strict lint cover the direct consumer boundary. No CLI currently consumes the new driver, so unrelated CLI capture test reruns, UI, capture/model/storage suites, whole Rust workspace, root aggregate and real storage qualification are out of scope. Changed behavioral production modules remain below 300 lines. Prior 294 evidence entries preserved. M17/M17.2 stay In progress. Configured startup, authoritative-storage lifetime/shutdown integration, broader rotation/root rebinding and discovery/delivery task-loss faults, Cursor/OpenCode readers, authenticated controls/coverage UI and real harness/cold acceptance remain pending; M17.3-M17.7 remain pending. The enabled server-startup guard is unchanged. No installed binaries/services, unrelated daemon restart, credentials, checkpoint, harness execution, deployment or publication changed. Final gates qualify four explicit runtime cases, 27 complete supervisor cases and eight underlying executor fault cases, owning/direct consumer compile and strict lint, Rust/document formatting, architecture/boundaries, canonical validation, spec-first and evidence bookkeeping. The configured foreground-server guard remains unchanged; no configured startup, real storage or cold harness qualification is claimed. Final review retains a bounded command sender inside the driver so internal failure latches terminal controls before drain. The new exact failed-dispatch test and all four previous runtime cases pass; final relevant count is 40 (five runtime, 27 supervisor and eight executor), with final all-target strict lint and Rust formatting passing. The final runtime module has 168 lines; supervisor remains 293. No unrelated source or contract changed."
  },
