    "versions": "Rust 1.98.1; JJ 0.45.1; macOS ARM64. Native MemoryStore, real loopback HTTP/private filesystem and fresh foreground subprocess; external S3 client without requests. Synthetic Codex CLI 0.156.1. No real RustFS/live harness acceptance.",
    "formats": "Additive installation-local GET /v1/local/capture and POST /v1/local/capture/control; actor-free version-1 command, opaque journal generation/revision and original durable receipt plus latest policy, replay and runtime request acceptance. Optional bootstrap local_capture_management. Existing device journal version 1, native AgentStore/source/spool/receipt formats unchanged.",
    "revision": "enclosing Jujutsu change xrxlnunl",
    "result": "pass",
    "remaining": [],
    "scope": "Current LocalTrusted Admin actor derives from transport. The manager revalidates bounded configuration and installation identity before private journal access and runtime application, binds one generation/control cell, and selects/replays latest policy under one retained owned blocking operation and filesystem gate across caller cancellation. A final bounded private binding/policy recheck withholds physical rebinding as unknown, retaining the original receipt for restored exact replay. Disabled/missing/stopped states cannot initialize, enable or restart capture. Durable receipt selection and runtime request acceptance stay separate. Shared public DTOs, HTTP config/router/contracts and response runner, journal callback and foreground control binding justify complete owning server/HTTP libraries, direct runtime/journal, all-target compile/strict lint for server/service/HTTP/CLI, every registered HTTP/SSE capture, generated web consumer and formatting/boundary/architecture/canonical/progress gates. This is the concrete escalation reason. Final product acceptance: 37 server-library and nine runtime entries in explicit serial execution, nine journal and five management integrations, 14 HTTP-library entries, all 147 actual registered HTTP/SSE responses, seven contract-tool cases and TypeScript fixture, generated web check and direct all-target compile/strict lint. Helpers are not independent behavior gates. Initial parallel runtime and cold-factory timeout failures remain recorded; exact cases and complete suites pass serially with every timeout, assertion and within-scenario concurrency unchanged. This is not a default-concurrency pass. Genuine absent-route and post-selection directory-rebinding regressions pass after repair; stale inventory is corrected against pinned parent schema plus exactly two added routes. No scanner, native format, observation bound or assertion changed for timing qualification. All prior 305 parsed evidence entries remain unchanged, total 306. Modified behavioral modules remain below 300 lines. Final document/canonical/progress sealing passes. M17/M17.2 remain In progress; rescan/import/source coverage and CLI/browser management, Cursor/OpenCode, remaining fault and real JJ/storage/live harness/cold full-flow qualification remain pending. M17.3-M17.7 remain Planned, with the whole goal active. The public configured automatic-startup guard stays. UI interaction/visual, root aggregates/full Rust workspace, real RustFS/live harness and unrelated suites are out of scope. Current AgentStore only; existing current V1 wire/device/source formats remain. No installation, migration, publication, deployment, credentials or unrelated daemon restart. A few canonical patch context misses applied no files. Narrow authenticated status/pause/resume slice complete; the next slice is rescan/import/coverage management."
  },
